Summary: They don't belong in net.sources

First off, apologies to those who know this posting doesn't belong here,
but note followups go to net.sources.d
Attention all those who post requests for sources to net.sources ...
PLEASE post your request in net.wanted.sources, where they belong.
Attention all those who want to report bugs, fixes, and the like ...
PLEASE post instead to net.sources.bugs or other more appropriate area.

In general, you should look at the list of news categories, and at the nature
of your posting, and post to the ONE category that most closely fits your
posting.  Why, do you say?  Well, many sites archive net.sources, and have
to go through and manually remove your improper posting, for one thing.

And a suggestion on your interminable requests for repostings ... if your
site missed posting 5/6 on the latest version of snazzo.c, first try to 
contact other nearby sites to see if they have it.  Probably someone in
the area archives such things; your system administrator can contact
neighboring sites to see which ones archive what categories.  If your
system admin. is too busy, try sending mail to userid usenet at your
immediate neighbor sites, preferably upstream from yours, as if your site
missed it, downstream probably did too.  If that route fails, then
make a posting to net.wanted.sources, with Distribution for your city
(for help here, see the sys. admin. again, or /usr/lib/news/distributions).
Give that a few days, then gradually move outwards in distributions.
And I would suggest that before you use Distribution: net that you try
sending mail directly to the original poster of snazzo.c.
Why all these steps, you ask?  It only takes a few seconds to send you
piddly request!  Well, multiply those few seconds by the number of sites
you'll be contacting, and you've run up quite a phone bill!

Thanks for your cooperation.  I'd like to see the quality of postings to
net.sources approach that of mod.sources, without having to have a moderator
to keep out all those poor postings.
